      "dimensions": {
        "A": "Necessary cash contract: finite number, zero retained. Refuses text/missing/nonfinite without coercion before the unchanged real Save caller. Formal red2 and final29 green; other content/wire validity and existing whole-GameState assertion remain unresolved, so file/card stay review.",
        "B": "savedAt ownership comment remains corrected; the new error identifies the corrupt money field. No SDLPal JSON format claim.",
        "C": "Validation stays in pure parser; DOM/FileReader in tools-panel and transaction/clone ownership in Save are unchanged. Existing overall as-GameState boundary still needs the wider contract.",
        "D": "One scalar guard, no helper/format migration/phase2 codec/default/upgrader. No duplicate persistence validation introduced.",
        "E": "Two new failure contracts: actual memory Save overwrite refusal plus independent nonfinite numeric literal. Zero is an explicit control; neighboring9 Save API tests pass. No browser/IndexedDB or complete schema credit.",
        "F": "Linear fail-fast field check, stable Chinese reason; no mode flag or nested decoder machinery added.",
        "G": "Both public exports and signatures preserved. Guard is necessary from actual malformed write; no new API/unused abstraction.",
        "H": "Pure parser remains deterministic; real memory Save can be isolated via its intended test reset and explicit no-indexedDB stub without mocking the parser or Save calls."
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "packages/game/src/tools/save-io.test.ts",
      "sha256": "57af1174768ed573d080b465856cc886dacaf19f6cdcaf90b0b136fdd55ceee7",
      "dimensions": {
        "A": "All seven cases read. Necessary-field rejection fixtures now begin with a real initial GameState and remove/change only the targeted field. Real-memory Save uses slot5, clears its map and restores globals after each case.",
        "B": "Titles distinguish corrupt cash, original slot retention, overflow and zero. Comment explicitly limits persistence proof to memory, excluding user IndexedDB.",
        "C": "Parser tests own header/value guards; real Save is exercised only for write-before-reject ordering. Quick-save timing remains in its canonical file.",
        "D": "Reuses actual Save and initial-state constructors; no serializer clone used as the only business oracle. Two legacy fixture fixes add no test identities.",
        "E": "Red:5pass/2fail, one Vitest rejects-expectation Error and one thrown-error AssertionError, both exact business mismatches. Green:7 parser +9 quick-save +4 toast +9 Save API=29, no pending/stderr. Literal prior scene4/cash55 and complete observed metadata preservation establish no overwrite. New cash test bodies unchanged after fixture repair.",
        "F": "Damaged property is visible in the fixture; overflow is injected into known serializer output with a checked substitution. No any/as-never or core mock added.",
        "G": "Two new tests correspond to the type and finite-number guard atoms; no coverage padding or weak success-only case. Current total20 includes the prior canonical consolidation; adjacent API adds9.",
        "H": "Explicit memory backend, actual async Save, no timers/network/browser storage. afterEach clears memory and restores the indexedDB global even after red failures."
      }
    }
